   guard that logs what it allowed and forgets what it refused cannot answer
   the only question an incident asks.
 
+  ## The fourth term: the grant is addressed, and the address is checked
+
+  `requested ∩ delegated ∩ local-policy` decides *what* may be reached. It
+  never decided *by whom*, and the gap was not that the datum was absent —
+  `:cap/holder` is one of `:identity-keys` in the language's semantics — but
+  that the answer was copied out of the request. A caller stating
+  `:cap/holder \"did:key:zWhoever\"` had that string arrive intact in the
+  capability handed to the handler, and no step between compared it to
+  anything. **The claim and the check were on the same side of the boundary.**
+
+  So `authorize` now takes `:holder` — the *authenticated* principal, the
+  sealed output of whatever ran the authentication (CACAO, passkey, a
+  verified DID proof, a parent capability). It is never read from
+  `requested`, and `requested`'s own `:cap/holder` is now ignored entirely
+  rather than propagated. A grant that names a holder is usable only by that
+  holder; a grant that names none is a bearer grant and says so out loud.
+
+  Bearer is still legitimate — a public read capability has no addressee —
+  but it becomes a decision rather than a default: `:policy/require-holder
+  true` in the local policy refuses one, the same shape
+  `:policy/forbid-wildcard` already uses to keep a lattice-legal value out of
+  production.
+
   ## No secret, anywhere
 
   The whole decision needs the token, the root **public** key, the local
@@ -38,9 +61,19 @@
   it to the semantics file rather than to a docstring."
   [:receipt/cap :receipt/at :receipt/call :receipt/outcome])
 
-(defn- receipt [{:keys [now call cap outcome detail]}]
+(defn- receipt [{:keys [now call cap outcome detail holder binding]}]
+  ;; `:receipt/holder` and `:receipt/holder-binding` are present on EVERY
+  ;; path, allowed and denied alike, and `:unauthenticated` is a distinct
+  ;; value from `:bearer`. "No principal was supplied" and "a principal was
+  ;; supplied and the grant did not ask for one" are different facts about a
+  ;; call, and a receipt that renders them identically cannot answer the only
+  ;; question an incident asks. They are extra keys, not additions to
+  ;; `receipt-keys`: `:receipt-requirements` is the floor the language sets,
+  ;; and a floor is not a ceiling.
   (cond-> {:receipt/at now :receipt/call call
-           :receipt/cap cap :receipt/outcome outcome}
+           :receipt/cap cap :receipt/outcome outcome
+           :receipt/holder holder
+           :receipt/holder-binding (or binding :unauthenticated)}
     detail (assoc :receipt/detail detail)))
 
 (defn- wildcard? [x] (or (= :any x) (= "*" x) (= :* x)))
@@ -50,20 +83,31 @@
 
   `{:semantics <capability-semantics map> :token t :root-public-key pk
     :verify-fn f :requested {:cap/kind k :cap/resource r} :local-policy p
-    :now instant :call name}`
+    :now instant :call name :holder principal-or-nil}`
+
+  `:holder` is the **authenticated** principal — the sealed result of an
+  authentication that already happened, handed in by the edge that ran it.
+  It is not a claim the caller makes about itself, and it is deliberately
+  not read from `requested`: `(:cap/holder requested)` is now ignored.
 
   -> `{:allowed? bool :reason kw :capability {…}|nil :receipt {…}}`
 
   The capability is only present when allowed, and it is the **concrete
   post-intersection** one (`:handler-receives`), never the token's claim."
-  [{:keys [semantics token root-public-key verify-fn requested local-policy now call]}]
+  [{:keys [semantics token root-public-key verify-fn requested local-policy now call holder]}]
   (let [rules (:rules semantics)
         kinds (:kinds semantics)
         {:cap/keys [kind resource]} requested
-        deny (fn [reason & [detail]]
+        ;; The request's own `:cap/holder` never leaves this function. It is
+        ;; dropped rather than compared, because comparing it would suggest
+        ;; it carried information: a caller asserting who it is tells you
+        ;; nothing you did not already have to establish elsewhere.
+        requested (dissoc requested :cap/holder)
+        deny (fn [reason & [{:keys [detail binding]}]]
                {:allowed? false :reason reason :capability nil
                 :receipt (receipt {:now now :call call :cap requested
-                                   :outcome :denied :detail (or detail reason)})})
+                                   :outcome :denied :detail (or detail reason)
+                                   :holder holder :binding binding})})
         v (bt/verify token root-public-key verify-fn)]
     (cond
       (not (:ok? v))
@@ -94,6 +138,12 @@
           (let [live (filter (fn [g] (let [e (:grant/expires g)]
                                        (or (nil? e) (neg? (compare now e)))))
                              matching)
+                ;; Token-scoped, like `before`: every grant folded out of one
+                ;; token carries the same addressee, so any live grant answers.
+                addressed-to (some :grant/holder live)
+                binding (cond (nil? addressed-to) (if holder :bearer :unauthenticated)
+                              (= addressed-to holder) :bound
+                              :else :mismatch)
                 delegated (into #{} (mapcat :grant/resources) live)
                 allowed (into #{} (:policy/allow local-policy))
                 ;; requested ∩ delegated ∩ local-policy, in that order and
@@ -103,17 +153,40 @@
                                                  (some wildcard? allowed))
                                            s #{})))]
             (cond
+              ;; The addressee is checked before the resource intersection so
+              ;; that a wrong holder is refused by its own name rather than
+              ;; disappearing into `:empty-intersection`. A denial that cannot
+              ;; say which term failed is a denial nobody can act on.
+              (and (some? addressed-to) (nil? holder))
+              (deny :holder-required {:binding :unauthenticated})
+
+              (= :mismatch binding)
+              (deny :wrong-holder {:binding :mismatch})
+
+              ;; Bearer stays legal, but production has to say so. Same shape
+              ;; as `:policy/forbid-wildcard`: the lattice permits it, the
+              ;; deployment declines it.
+              (and (:policy/require-holder local-policy) (nil? addressed-to))
+              (deny :unbound-grant {:binding binding})
+
               (and (:policy/forbid-wildcard local-policy)
                    (or (some wildcard? delegated) (wildcard? resource)))
-              (deny :production-effective-wildcard)
+              (deny :production-effective-wildcard {:binding binding})
 
               (and (= :deny (:empty-intersection rules)) (empty? effective))
-              (deny :empty-intersection)
+              (deny :empty-intersection {:binding binding})
 
               :else
-              (let [cap {:cap/kind kind :cap/resource resource
-                         :cap/holder (:cap/holder requested)
-                         :cap/provenance :biscuit}]
+              ;; `:cap/holder` is the AUTHENTICATED principal or absent. It is
+              ;; never `(:cap/holder requested)` — that value was dropped on
+              ;; entry — and it is omitted rather than set to nil, because
+              ;; `kotoba.lang.capability-values` validates the key when the key
+              ;; is present and a nil there is a malformed capability, not an
+              ;; unaddressed one.
+              (let [cap (cond-> {:cap/kind kind :cap/resource resource
+                                 :cap/provenance :biscuit}
+                          holder (assoc :cap/holder holder))]
                 {:allowed? true :reason :granted :capability cap
                  :receipt (receipt {:now now :call call :cap cap
-                                    :outcome :allowed})}))))))))
+                                    :outcome :allowed
+                                    :holder holder :binding binding})}))))))))
diff --git a/src/biscuit/kotoba.cljc b/src/biscuit/kotoba.cljc
